# WENGE-0001 / SPEC-0001 A1. Stop must not leave a note ringing in the receiver.
# Ref: CE v5.30 is silent on what Stop does to a note that is still sounding (p.94 covers
# only the second press of Stop). Reading chosen: every sounding note gets a NoteOff and
# CC 123 goes out on each channel that had one. See AMBIGUITIES.md "stop with sounding notes".
#
# Two long notes on two ports: track 0 on port 1 channel 1, track 3 on port 2 channel 4.
seed 1
bpm 120
page.tracks 0,3 enabled
track 0 mch 1
track 3 mch 20
track 0 step 0 len 192
track 3 step 0 len 192
play
# 14 buffers of 512 is 7,168 samples: the first step has fired, and its 192-tick note (a whole
# note, 96,000 samples) is far from over.
render 14 buffers buffer=512
expect event on port=1 ch=1 count=1
expect event on port=2 ch=4 count=1
expect event off absent
stop
render 1 buffers buffer=512
# The flush lands at sample 0 of the render that follows the stop.
expect event off port=1 ch=1 count=1 at=7168
expect event off port=2 ch=4 count=1 at=7168
expect event cc cc=123 port=1 ch=1 count=1 at=7168
expect event cc cc=123 port=2 ch=4 count=1 at=7168
expect event cc cc=123 count=2
expect balance
# Nothing more happens while stopped.
clear events
render 100 buffers buffer=512
expect event on absent
expect event off absent
expect event cc absent
